<section class="faq-page section-spacing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-header reveal">
      <h1 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="faq-subtitle">Everything you need to know about our miners, shipping, and support.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-sections">
      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Our Products &amp; Service</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Are miners tested before shipping?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes — every unit undergoes a 24-hour burn-in test, full hashrate validation, and thermal benchmarking before it leaves our facility. We only ship hardware we'd deploy ourselves.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Do miners include power supplies?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Miners are sold without a PSU unless specifically listed as a bundle. We carry compatible APW12 power supplies separately. Check the individual product listing for what's included.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What firmware options are available?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>We offer miners pre-flashed with stock firmware, Vnish, or Braiins OS+ — just specify at checkout or contact sales. Vnish delivers powerful overclocking tools, while Braiins OS+ optimizes efficiency and auto-tuning. Custom firmware configuration is also available for wholesale orders.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Are products surplus or refurbished?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Our inventory is <strong>tested surplus</strong> — genuine manufacturer hardware sourced from verified channels, not rebuilt or repaired units marketed as refurbished. Every piece passes our full benchmark suite before we list it. Condition notes are included on each product page.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Shipping &amp; Orders</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How fast do orders ship?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Most orders ship within 48 hours from our USA warehouse. Freight shipping for larger orders typically arrives in 3–5 business days domestically. Tracking is provided for every shipment.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Do you ship internationally?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Currently we ship within the USA only. International shipping may be available for large wholesale orders — contact sales for details.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What warranty do you offer?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>All units include a 30-day warranty covering DOA and manufacturing defects. Extended warranty options are available for wholesale orders.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Wholesale &amp; Bulk Orders</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Do you offer wholesale pricing?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. Wholesale pricing is available starting at 10+ units, with our best rates on pallet quantities (40–50 units). Submit a quote request on our <a href="/pages/wholesale" class="faq-link">Wholesale page</a> or contact sales directly.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Can I request bulk inventory?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Absolutely. We maintain pallet-quantity stock across our most popular ASIC models and can source specific configurations on request. Fill out the inquiry form on our <a href="/pages/wholesale" class="faq-link">Wholesale page</a> with the model, hashrate, and quantity you need and our team will respond within 4 hours.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Can you help with facility deployments?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes! We offer deployment consulting, firmware configuration, and ongoing engineering support for facility-scale operations. Talk to our team to get started.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Firmware &amp; Tuning</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What's the difference between Vnish and Braiins OS?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Both replace stock firmware. Vnish provides advanced overclocking controls, while Braiins OS+ focuses on efficiency and auto-tuning. Both can be pre-flashed on request.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>Can I tune my miner for efficiency?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes — custom firmware supports tuning profiles for efficiency (lower power draw) or performance (higher hashrate). Our engineers can help configure optimal settings for your operation.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-section reveal">
        <h2 class="faq-section-title">Power &amp; Infrastructure</h2>
        <div class="faq-group">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What electrical requirements do I need?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>You'll need 220–240V power circuits with adequate amperage (typically 15–20A per miner). Consult an electrician for facility-scale deployments.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>How loud are these miners?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>ASIC miners run at 70–80 dB. They are not suitable for residential use and require a dedicated space with proper ventilation and noise isolation.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span>What's the difference between hashrate models?</span>
              <svg class="faq-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Higher hashrate (TH/s) means more mining throughput. An S19 XP 140TH outperforms an S19 Pro 110TH but draws more power. Efficiency (J/TH) is equally important — we list both specs on every product.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-cta reveal">
      <div class="faq-cta-card glass">
        <h2>Didn't find your answer?</h2>
        <p>Our team is here to help with any questions about hardware, setup, or wholesale orders.</p>
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn btn-premium">Contact Support</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

